# Git: `dev` daily, `main` on deploy

- **`dev`** = all day-to-day commits and pushes. Stay here.
- **`main`** = production. Touch only when the user says deploy / promote / ship.

Never create or switch branches (no `fix/*`, no cloud/`auto-*`) unless the user names the branch in this message. Never revert/reset commits unless asked.

Daily: commit when asked → `git push -u origin HEAD` on `dev`.
Deploy (user-asked only): push `dev`, then promote `dev` → `main` (fast-forward push or PR). No feature branches.
